zo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schenk</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Spillmann</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Klipstein</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Relationship between perceived exertion and mean power frequency of the EMG signal from the upper trapezius muscle during isometric shoulder elevation</article-title><source>Eur J Appl Physiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>321</fpage><lpage>326</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s00421-005-0014-7</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hummel A, La&#x000fc;bli T, Pozzo M, Schenk P, Spillmann S, Klipstein A (2005) Relationship between perceived exertion and mean power frequency of the EMG signal from the upper trapezius muscle during isometric shoulder elevation. Eur J Appl Physiol 95:321&#x02013;326 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16096843</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>SK</given-names></name><name><surname>Rochette</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ortega</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Enoka</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Task differences with the same load torque alter the endurance time of submaximal fatiguing contractions in humans</article-title><source>J Neurophysiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>88</volume><fpage>3087</fpage><lpage>3096</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1152/jn.00232.2002</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hunter SK, Rochette DL, Ortega JD, Enoka RM (2002) Task differences with the same load torque alter the endurance time of submaximal fatiguing contractions in humans. J Neurophysiol 88:3087&#x02013;3096 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12466432</pub-id></citation></r